WEBVTT

00:00:09,070 --> 00:00:15,950
If a person is using the RIFE machine for Lyme disease, why do they react so severely

00:00:15,950 --> 00:00:21,950
and what should they do to prevent Herc's reactions?

00:00:21,950 --> 00:00:36,470
So a Herc cyber reaction is a reaction because you are reacting to the die-off of a bacteria.

00:00:36,470 --> 00:00:45,950
So with gram-negative bacteria like Borrelia burgodorophy, it has lipopolysaccharides in the cell

00:00:45,950 --> 00:00:53,110
membrane of that bacteria, and then when you kill it, it liberates those lipopolysaccharides

00:00:53,110 --> 00:00:58,190
and lipopolysaccharides can damage the blood barrier across the blood barrier and cause

00:00:58,190 --> 00:00:59,590
inflammation of the brain.

00:00:59,590 --> 00:01:07,590
If you already have primed microglial cells, you will experience all sorts of reactions

00:01:07,590 --> 00:01:13,310
and symptoms that have been come to note as a Herc cyber reaction.

00:01:13,310 --> 00:01:16,510
So what could you do about it?

00:01:16,510 --> 00:01:20,590
You have to just go slower with your treatment.

00:01:20,590 --> 00:01:31,030
So slower with your treatment means either you run less time on the program or you move

00:01:31,030 --> 00:01:36,070
the bulb farther away from you so there will be less effect on your body.

00:01:36,070 --> 00:01:41,310
So I have had some Lyme patients actually have to put the machine in the bulb in the adjacent

00:01:41,310 --> 00:01:45,230
room because they react so severely.

00:01:45,230 --> 00:01:49,710
But typically, if you put it in the other side of the room, then if you cover it with

00:01:49,710 --> 00:01:54,190
the pillow of the bulb, of course it's going to go through the pillow, but it's going

00:01:54,190 --> 00:02:01,070
to disperse some farther away from the bulb, the less treatment effect it will have on

00:02:01,070 --> 00:02:02,070
your body.

00:02:02,070 --> 00:02:04,070
So the thing is that we recommend.

